# A Claude Code user with two skills: one user-invocable (a slash command)
# and one meant only for the model to consult (user-invocable: false).
# Kiln invokes skills only as slash commands, so the model-only skill is an
# expected gap.
@real
@home scratch
@size 140x45
@fixture qa/fixtures/real/ext-skills

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 30
TYPE /rel
WAIT 1
SHOT slash-palette
EXPECT /release-notes/
EXPECT_NOT /api-conventions/
KEY backspace
TURN /release-notes
SHOT release-notes-done
TURN Add a GET /health endpoint to app.py that returns {"status": "ok"}, following our API conventions.
SHOT health-endpoint-done
RUN grep -q 'X-Api-Version' {PROJ}/app.py
NOTE expected gap: api-conventions is user-invocable:false, meant for the model to consult on its own, but kiln only exposes skills as slash commands (the model cannot invoke a skill itself) — the RUN check above (the convention the skill alone states) is expected to fail.
